{"author":{"id":"836d943203cf5a4f01ab5d4b4780de84949c43734f2256a167cc5931ae5d8c66"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794172786,"nonce":"0uxLixXOkFtskWSpWOLk71r8ePw=","title":"L7 — Write actions: close, reopen, state, comment","message":"## Context\nThe app is read-only. Port `gb`'s write semantics so the app never disagrees with the roadmap plugin.\n\n## Files\n- `src/gitbug/cli.rs` — write fns\n- `src/ui/detail.rs` — action buttons + comment box; row context actions\n\n## Approach\n- Only full ids reach git-bug (`../skillforge/plugins/roadmap/skills/gb/scripts/lib/gb_core.sh:45-62`).\n- `close`: drop all `state:*` labels, then `git-bug bug status close \u003cid\u003e`; no-op when closed (`../skillforge/plugins/roadmap/skills/gb/scripts/gb:358-366`).\n- `reopen`: `git-bug bug status open \u003cid\u003e` only when closed (`gb:368-374`).\n- `set_state(InProgress | Blocked | Clear)`: refuse on closed; remove other `state:*`, add target if missing — only send the label diff, git-bug exits 1 otherwise (`gb:313-356`).\n- `comment`: `git-bug bug comment new \u003cid\u003e --message=\u003cbody\u003e --non-interactive`; never `-F`, it strips `#` headings (`gb:206-209`, `gb:305-311`). Reject empty bodies.\n- After a write, re-read that issue and update state; show errors (incl. `Locked`) inline.\n\n## Depends on\nL6 — detail pane\n\n## Out of scope\n- Create/edit title/body, label editing beyond `state:`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- Tests against a temp repo with a real git-bug identity (`git-bug user new ... --non-interactive`), skipped with a printed reason when `git-bug` is absent: close drops `state:*` labels, state switch leaves exactly one `state:*`, comment keeps `## headings`\n- All three gates pass","files":null}]}